<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Aduatuci</h1><p class="st-meta">110 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Belgic people said to descend from Cimbri and Teutones, whose entire population was sold into slavery by Caesar in 57 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Caesar says the Aduatuci descended from six thousand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimbri">Cimbri</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutones">Teutones</a> left to guard the baggage of the great migration before 102 BCE, who settled on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a>. Their stronghold is usually placed near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-namur">Namur</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuin">Thuin</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium">Belgium</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They imposed tribute on their neighbours, including the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eburones">Eburones</a>, and fortified a hilltop oppidum.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 57 BCE they surrendered to Caesar but attacked his camp at night with hidden weapons. Caesar stormed the oppidum and sold the inhabitants, fifty-three thousand by his count, into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. Survivors joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambiorix">Ambiorix</a> in 54 BCE, after which the name disappears.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/aduatuci.jpg" alt="Aduatuci" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: User:Feitscherg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Gallia_Tribes_Towns.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>110 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Belgium</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Atuatuci</dd></dl></aside></div>

